# data.zd — the parts of the home page that are prose rather than files.
#
# The blog and the projects are read off disk, because they are documents.
# These four sections are not: `now` is five lines that change when life
# does, `range` is thirteen domains, and neither has ever wanted a file of
# its own. They are `static` lists here, which is the same placement the
# posts get and the same cost — the build host holds them and the reader is
# handed the answer.

record Line
    label  is Text
    title  is Text
    detail is Text

# `~/portfolio $ cat now.txt`. `Line`, not `Line`: `Line` is a route
# variant in `blog.zd`, and a route variant and a record share one namespace.
state now is static List of Line starting [(Line with label is "building", title is "JudgeHuman", detail is "a crowd sourced alignment research platform, now becoming a company"), (Line with label is "also shipping", title is "AppMeee", detail is "the unified inbox, fourteen platforms and counting"), (Line with label is "reading", title is "inference and context engineering papers", detail is "KV cache management, context rot, and what distillation actually transfers"), (Line with label is "away from the desk", title is "learning to jump a mountain bike", detail is "badly, and with great enthusiasm"), (Line with label is "working at", title is "go find some cat fish foo!", detail is ""), (Line with label is "studied", title is "M.Eng in Computer Science, Cornell University", detail is "campus located somewhere in dream world")]

state about is static List of Text starting ["I'm Mark, a generalist who'd rather build the thing than pick a lane.", "The work moved and I followed it. Products increasingly meant AI products, and doing one of those properly turns out to require knowing what sits underneath, so I went and found out. A transformer written from scratch shows you what the architecture does. The autodifferentiation beneath it shows you why that works. Hand scheduling its kernels in a compiler shows you where the time actually goes, which is a different discipline again. Cornell coursework in ML hardware and systems, natural language processing and deep generative models put theory under what I had been learning by hand.", "All of that is an argument for range rather than against it. The Rust servers, the iOS apps and the infrastructure are not a detour from the AI work — knowing a lot of things is the job now, and the people who only know the model layer find that out the hard way. Several projects here are being rebuilt at the moment, deliberately: ship, learn, rebuild better."]

# Thirteen domains, each a name, what it covers, and what it is written in.
# `domains`, not `range`: the prelude has a `range` and a prelude name
# cannot be shadowed. The same collision the language changelog warns about,
# met from the other side.
state domains is static List of Line starting [(Line with label is "Machine Learning", title is "transformers built from scratch, continual learning, generative models", detail is "Python · PyTorch"), (Line with label is "ML Systems & Compilers", title is "hand written TVM schedules, GPU kernels, CPU and FPGA targets", detail is "TVM · CUDA · TensorIR"), (Line with label is "Natural Language Processing", title is "classifiers without a library, feature design, error analysis", detail is "Python · NumPy"), (Line with label is "AI Agents", title is "agent labor markets, verdict platforms, autonomous workers", detail is "TypeScript · Gemini · Agents"), (Line with label is "Systems", title is "E2EE messaging servers, protocol tooling, game loops", detail is "Rust · Swift"), (Line with label is "Mobile", title is "voice social apps, native iMessage integration", detail is "Swift · SwiftUI"), (Line with label is "Web & Backend", title is "microservices and monorepos, simulation pipelines, unified inboxes, Python services", detail is "TypeScript · Bun · Node · Flask"), (Line with label is "Cloud & Orchestration", title is "services on AWS and Google Cloud, Kubernetes clusters, object storage and CDN, infrastructure as code", detail is "AWS · GCP · Kubernetes · Terraform"), (Line with label is "Self-Hosting", title is "homeserver fleets, reproducible deploys, bridge networks", detail is "Ansible · Docker · Matrix"), (Line with label is "Security & Crypto", title is "end to end encryption by default, bridged E2EE, key handling", detail is "Rust · Matrix"), (Line with label is "Simulation & Games", title is "MCTS decision engines, market models, space economies", detail is "Rust · Python"), (Line with label is "The Day Job", title is "large scale services at a place that shall not be named", detail is "Java · C++ · Go"), (Line with label is "Off Hours", title is "browser games, childhood MMO nostalgia, terminal easter eggs", detail is "TypeScript · Canvas")]
